;================================================================
; BASILISK
; BYZANTINE ADAPTIVE COUNTERWEIGHT AI
;
; IDENTITY
;   1v1 standard-land competitive heuristic controller.
;   Persistent strategic intent. Adaptive counter-composition.
;   Practical engine-native execution. Bounded recovery.
;   The opponent's commitment is information, not destiny.
;
; NAME
;   BASILISK is the project's combat metaphor: observe the commitment,
;   answer it with the cheapest credible counter, preserve pressure,
;   and punish the next commitment when the position permits it.
;================================================================
; BASILISK // BYZANTINE ADAPTIVE COUNTERWEIGHT AI
; FINAL INTEGRATED COMPETITIVE CONTROLLER
;
; PURPOSE
;   Execute a practical 1v1 standard-land Byzantine strategy while retaining
;   community-native .per discipline and engine-native reliability.
;
; CONTROL LOOP
;
;   SCOUT
;      ->
;   OBSERVE
;      ->
;   STRATEGY-GOAL
;      ->
;   UNIT-GOAL
;      ->
;   PRODUCTION ARBITRATION
;      ->
;   ARMY GATHERING
;      ->
;   ATTACK
;      ->
;   RETREAT IF NEEDED
;      ->
;   REASSESS
;
; COMMUNITY-STYLE CONSTANTS
;
;   attack-goal       = 2
;   strategy-goal     = 3
;   unit-goal         = 4
;   train-civ-goal    = 5
;   sn-resource-control = 191
;
;   flush = 200
;   rush  = 201
;   boom  = 202
;   mix   = 1
;
;   scouting timer = 3
;   attack timer   = 4
;   retreat timer  = 15
;
;   group-type-land-explore = 101
;
; IMPORTANT
;   This is a standalone competitive controller.
;   Do not load another controller that defines the same constants,
;   goals, timers, or owns the same strategy/unit-production state.
;
; REMOVE OLD DIRECT MILITARY TRAIN RULES
;
;   Old architecture:
;       enemy cavalry -> train spear
;       enemy archers -> train skirm
;       enemy spears  -> train archer
;
;   New architecture:
;       enemy observation
;           ->
;       strategy-goal
;           ->
;       unit-goal
;           ->
;       centralized military production
;
;================================================================
;================================================================
(include "BasiliskTelemetry.xs")
;
; 0. ENGINE / COMMUNITY DEFINITIONS
;================================================================
; Q: "What is sn-resource-control?"
;
; Strategic number 191.
; It is the resource-claim register used by established .per AIs.
;
; Controller semantics:
;
;   0            = no strategic claim
;   feudal-age   = Feudal claim owns the bank
;   castle-age   = Castle claim owns the bank
;   imperial-age = Imperial claim owns the bank
;   ri-*         = technology owns the bank only for the start action; the
;                  global claim is released immediately after research is issued
;
(defconst sn-resource-control 191)
; Documented DE strategic-number alias used by the intelligent gathering handoff.
(defconst sn-intelligent-gathering 142)
; DE Siege Tower has no built-in AI identifier in the AIRef object table.
; Its Definitive Edition object id is 1105; define the local symbol before counting it.
(defconst siege-tower 1105)
; Logistica is a DE-only research alias absent from the scraped AI name registry.
; Community AI references define the research id explicitly as 61 before use.
(defconst ri-logistica 61)
; Build-185872 regional-unit upgrade. Current parsed DE game data identifies
; tech 1454 as Elite Varangian Guard (2703 -> 2704). Keep it local until
; the active AIRef registry exposes a named ri-* alias.
(defconst ri-elite-varangian-guard 1454)
; Update 185872 Byzantine regional infantry. These are site-specific
; train targets, so keep the exact numeric IDs local until AIRef exposes
; a native named line in the active DE registry.
(defconst varangian-guard 2703)
(defconst elite-varangian-guard 2704)

; Varangian Guard response package.
; Demand is premium cavalry-response intent; target/fielded are derived state.
(defconst bt-varangian-demand-goal 726)
(defconst bt-varangian-target-goal 727)
(defconst bt-varangian-fielded-goal 728)
(defconst bt-varangian-count-scratch-goal 800)
; Persistent friendly-army witnesses for blacksmith technology policy.
(defconst bt-blacksmith-ranged-army-goal 801)
(defconst bt-blacksmith-infantry-army-goal 802)
(defconst bt-varangian-target-level-2 4)
(defconst bt-varangian-target-level-3 6)
(defconst bt-varangian-logistica-min 6)
; Elite upgrade policy: 750F/475G is too expensive for a six-Guard army.
; Twelve committed Guards amortize the upgrade to roughly one Guard-equivalent
; of food/gold per existing Guard and fit the Imperial premium-package role.
(defconst bt-varangian-elite-target-level 12)

; VARANGIAN INTEGRATION CHECKLIST
;   1. Exact unit symbols: 2703 / 2704.
;   2. Persistent demand: cavalry pressure -> finite target.
;   3. Completion witness: queue-inclusive regular+elite total.
;   4. Execution: Barracks + can-train-with-escrow -> train.
;   5. Resource arbitration: premium-gold mode protects the package.
;   6. Upgrade continuation: six Guards can earn shared Logistica.
;   7. Release: cavalry pressure/target/premium-tech completion clears demand.
;   8. Existing cheap Spear/Camel counters remain the first response tier.

